\nUndergraduate plus Master\u2019s Degree Programmes\nOpportunities\nStudents Exchange\nInternships\nAwards\nScholarships\nTeaching and Research Facilities\nLife\nCompetitions\nHonor Society\nStudent Chapter\nSoft Skills\nCareer\nCompany Visits\nJob Opportunities\nResearch Degree\nAim\nAdmission\nApplication\nCurriculum\nOur Graduates\nContact Us\nApplication Procedure\nAdmission to our PhD programme can be processed through Normal Round and Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (https://www.cityu.edu.hk/pg/hong-kong-phd-fellowship-scheme).\nTo Apply:\n(1) Getting Started - Look for research areas and take TOEFL/IELTS\n(2) Preparation - Contact a potential supervisor and write an original research proposal for HKPFS.\n(3) Submit - Through CityUHK's Online Admission System and the RGC's Online Application System for HKPFS.\n(4) Checklist for applicant (pdf).\nApplication Deadline\nApplication Procedure\nHKPFS\n1 Dec 2026 (by 12:00 noon Hong Kong Time)\nSubmit an initial application at the RGC's Online Application System (OAS) to obtain a RGC reference number.\nhttp://www.rgc.edu.hk/hkphd\n1 Dec 2026\nSubmit a full application to CityUHK's Online Admission System with supporting documents, complete the \u201cHK PhD Fellowship Scheme\u201d tab, and quote the RGC reference number.\nhttps://www.cityu.edu.hk/pg/research-degree-programmes/steps-and-procedures\nNormal Round\n1 Dec 2026\nSubmit a full application to CityUHK's Online Admission System with supporting documents.\nhttps://www.cityu.edu.hk/pg/research-degree-programmes/steps-and-procedures\n*Although admission is mainly considered in the normal admission round, applications are accepted throughout the year. Early admission may be given to outstanding candidates.\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme\nWith the aim to recruit the brightest students in the world to pursue their PhD studies in Hong Kong, the Government of Hong Kong has established the Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS). The application deadline is listed in the table above. Applicants are required to submit to both RGC's Online Application System (OAS) and CityUHK's Online Admission System.\nThe call for application is set for 1 September 2026 (at 12 noon GMT +8h).\nHKPFS from the Hong Kong government\u2019s Research Grants Council (RGC) provides a monthly stipend of HK$344,400 (~ US$44,150), and conference and research-related travel allowance of HK$14,400 (~US$1,840) per year for the awardees for a maximum of three years. (CityUHK will provide the same level of monthly studentship to cover the fourth year of studies.)\nCityUHK\u2019s HKPFS recipients are awarded the \u201cChow Yei Ching School of Graduate Studies Entrance Scholarship\u201d (HK$95,496 (~US$12,243), which covers students' tuition and on-campus hostel accommodation fees in their first year of research studies.\nHKPFS applicants will also be considered for the Normal Round admission to CityUHK. For applicants selected by CityUHK to RGC, firm admission offers with regular postgraduate studentship will be given by CityUHK, even if they are not awarded HKPFS by RGC at the end.\nThe admission offer will be confirmed by CityUHK in January 2027. HKPFS results will be announced by RGC in March 2027.\nFor any amendments to a submitted application in the CityUHK Online Admission System, please contact the EE Department or Chow Yei Ching School of Graduate Studies for assistance.\nNormal Round Admission\nApplicants are required to submit a full application to CityUHK's Online Admission System. The application deadline for the Normal Round is listed in the table above. Applicants are encouraged to contact a potential supervisor prior to submitting an application to our university. While it is not mandatory for applicant to contact EE faculty prior to submitting an application, they must declare an research area of interest in the application form. See checklist for further details on choosing a research area.\nLast Updated: 27 Oct 2025\nAbout Us\nVision & Mission